      ],
      "source": "https://williamscreek.org/our-history-1",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Great Depression, road maintenance faltered due to a shrinking tax base, prompting residents to incorporate in 1931.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://williamscreek.org/our-history-1",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Williams Creek became part of Indianapolis in 1970 under Unigov yet keeps its own town government.",
